{"type":"message","id":"68710082","parentId":"79a0e553","timestamp":"2026-04-22T06:40:07.922Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The issue is with PowerShell variable syntax. In PowerShell, `$env:VARIABLE_NAME` is used to reference environment variables, but the syntax for setting them inline is different. Let me try a different approach with `;` separator.\n\nActually the issue is that when passing to `powershell -Command`, the `$` gets interpreted by the outer shell. Let me use proper quoting.\n\nWait, actually the error shows the `$env:` part was stripped and it tried to execute `=sk-cp-...`. This means the `$` was not escaped properly.\n\nIn PowerShell, to set an env var inline you'd use:\n`$env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY='value'; command`\n\nBut when called from cmd/PowerShell context, we need to escape the `$` sign since it's already in a string. Let me try using double quotes and escaping or using a different approach.","thinkingSignature":"f98dc1f68fc3e2b584101a47606f5753bb159a2b3e6e8471ebad6f621127e5eb"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_atu9236fuxma_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"powershell -Command \"Set-Item -Path 'Env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY' -Value 'sk-cp-5i5B9H8es37BzpuBXF2fbCiuIVfyHMfAcefazgd91NVeDUCU9o22qQCH7AsdZ4mWDjQ9i-LkfAo6gMe1UbUlE1W64U7oAvI2ZlHf0TLrvsXXEwmTlRNDM-M'; claude -p 'hello'\"","timeout":30}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":8151,"output":330,"cacheRead":32834,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":41315,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1776839995787,"responseId":"0637a03c6ef08d976921dd95e0757be3"}}
